  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through Monday)\nIssued at 1132 PM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nNear persistent conditions will continue through mid week and \ntoward the weekend as an extensive surface ridge axis extends\nsouthwestward from southwestern Canada into northeast Oklahoma. \nDry weather will largely prevail through the work week as mid \nlevel ridging builds back over much of the Southern Plains. This \nwill lead to mostly sunny days with a slow, but steady warmup as \nwe near the weekend. Another system could clip the local region \nthis weekend as the ridge shifts southward, bringing some more \nrain chances and a slight cooldown. Signals point to a \npotentially more active pattern heading into the next week with \nmore widespread rain chances and a more seasonably significant \ncold front potentially on the horizon. We will have to wait and \nsee how that plays out in the coming days.\n\nBowlan",
